<%= render layout: "admin/shared/record_page",
           locals: { title: transaction_title(@portfolio_transaction),
                     breadcrumbs: @breadcrumbs,
                     description: transaction_summary(@portfolio_transaction),
                     actions: capture do
                       # A Ruby comment, not an ERB one: this is inside a `capture` block, and a comment tag
                       # inside another tag ends it mid-expression - a trap this repo has recorded four times.
                       #
                       # Only where the record is still valid. A failed save re-renders this page with the
                       # attributes the user submitted, so an invalid transaction has no portfolio to name, and
                       # the confirmation names one.
                       if @portfolio_transaction.portfolio.present?
                         link_to "Delete transaction",
                                 admin_portfolio_transaction_path(@portfolio_transaction),
                                 data: { turbo_method: :delete,
                                         turbo_confirm: transaction_delete_confirm(@portfolio_transaction) },
                                 class: admin_danger_button_class
                       end
                     end } do %>
  <%# **Four cards became one section.** "Portfolio", "Transaction details" and "Description" were all
      attributes the form edits - portfolio, type, reason, amount, description - displayed a second time where
      they could not be changed. The two facts the form cannot express are the **date** the money moved and the
      **order** that caused it, and both are one line each, so they are the summary rather than sections of
      their own. That is the same rule the stock page's holders line follows.

      The title was "Portfolio transaction #215". An id is not a name, and design.md already records moving
      that id to the breadcrumb on this very page - so the heading says what the transaction *is*. %>
  <%= render layout: "admin/shared/record_section",
             locals: { title: "Details", hint: "Saved when you press Update transaction." } do %>
    <%= render "form", portfolio_transaction: @portfolio_transaction %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
